Short:        Source of the OFS/FFS to PFS3 converter
Author:       terriblefire
Uploader:     stephen@terriblefire.com (terriblefire)
Type:         disk/misc
Version:      0.3
Architecture: generic

ffs2pfs source
==============

The source of ffs2pfs, which converts an OFS or FFS hard disk partition
to PFS3 in place, keeping every file, and survives a power cut at any
moment. The program is in disk/misc/ffs2pfs.lha; its readme says what it
does and how to use it.


Files
-----

  ffs2pfs-src/c/          the converter: the core (no AmigaOS calls),
                          amiga.c (the Shell), gui.c (the window,
                          GadTools) and host.c (for the tests)
  ffs2pfs-src/tests/      the test harnesses (Python), and tests/amidisk/,
                          the readers they check images with (RDB, FFS,
                          PFS3)
  ffs2pfs-src/check/      reads converted images with the real pfs3aio
                          handler (through AmiFUSE)
  ffs2pfs-src/tools/      test image makers; amiga/crcwalk.c lists the
                          CRC of every file on a volume
  ffs2pfs-src/ref/        pfs3aio 19.2, which the program carries, and
                          its licence
  ffs2pfs-src/README.md   the full documentation: how it works, and the
                          tests and their results


Building
--------

The Amiga binary is cross-compiled with vbcc and the NDK 3.2; the host
build (the same converter on a disk image file, for the tests) needs gcc:

  make -C c ffs2pfs NDK32=/path/to/NDK3.2
  make -C c f2p_host

The Makefile turns ref/pfs3aio into C data with xxd. The program is
built with -cpu=68000 and runs on every Amiga with Kickstart 2.04 or
later.


Testing
-------

The tests cut a conversion off after every single block write, also with
the last write torn, and check that it then either finishes or rolls
back to the FFS volume it was, with every file intact. README.md has the
suites and their results.


